  "worked_solution": "Let's first add an ${X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $16$ | $4$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third rows of our table, we can immediately conclude that \n\n$$\nP({X}^{2}=4)=0.2+0.3=0.5.\n$$",
